## Latest Reported Global EV Sales Figures for 2026

As of late July 2026, the most recent fully reported global sales data covers **June 2026**, while complete July figures have not yet been compiled.

### June 2026 Single-Month Performance
- **Global sales:** 2.0 million battery-electric and plug-in hybrid vehicles. [1](#f0ad0c80-71f1-4ac7-8cb7-432590b6264c) [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)
- **Year-over-year growth:** +7% compared to June 2025. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)
- **Month-over-month growth:** +11% from May 2026. [5](#f0ad0c80-71f1-4ac7-8cb7-432590b6264c)
- **Trend:** June marked the fourth consecutive month of rising global EV demand. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)

### First-Half 2026 Year-to-Date Performance
- **Cumulative global sales:** 9.6 million units through June 2026. [1](#f0ad0c80-71f1-4ac7-8cb7-432590b6264c) [2](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)
- **Year-over-year growth:** +2% compared to the first half of 2025. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec) [2](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)

### Regional Breakdown for June 2026
- **Europe:** Led all regions with approximately 530,000 registrations, a 31% year-over-year surge that set a new June record. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec) The region accounted for roughly 2.5 million EV sales during the first half of the year and remains the primary engine of global growth. [3](#f0ad0c80-71f1-4ac7-8cb7-432590b6264c)
- **China:** Registered about 1.0 million units in June, down 11% from the prior year amid weaker domestic demand. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec) Despite the monthly decline, China still comprised 51% of global EV sales through the first half of 2026. [2](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)
- **North America:** Registrations fell 13% in June as the U.S. market continued to adjust following the elimination of federal EV tax credits. [12](#f7c0544a-e57f-461a-af04-4eb34aefa1ec)

### Historical Context and 2026 Outlook
- **2025 baseline:** Full-year 2025 was a record-breaking milestone, with global EV sales exceeding 20 million units for the first time. [1](#638246ff-f0b6-4229-a9b8-3b97cb211c7d) [2](#638246ff-f0b6-4229-a9b8-3b97cb211c7d)
- **2026 projection:** Industry outlooks currently forecast around **23 million** global EV sales for the full year 2026, though this remains a projection rather than reported data. [4](#f0ad0c80-71f1-4ac7-8cb7-432590b6264c)

